"ATTRIBUTES_SMART_WORKER_PROMPT","53","asset","asset_inspection","92","The output provides comprehensive coverage of asset inspection attributes aligned with NCDOT's operational context, including bridge inspections (NBIS standards), pavement inspections (PCI, IRI, PSI), and general asset management. The schema includes 78 attributes covering identification, inspector details, location, condition ratings, defects, corrective actions, compliance, costs, and system integration fields. All attributes follow naming conventions (snake_case, no product prefix except for PK), proper data types, appropriate PII tagging (inspector names, team members), and relevant regulatory references (NBIS, AASHTO, FHWA, MUTCD, SAP PM). The model aligns with SAP PM and ATLAS systems mentioned in the operational systems of record. Minor uncertainty exists around the optimal balance between bridge-specific attributes (deck/superstructure/substructure ratings) and general asset inspection attributes, but this is a reasonable judgment call given the consolidation note mentioning bridge.inspection. The attribute count (78) falls within the suggested range and represents genuine business value without filler. All previous feedback has been addressed as this is the initial generation."
