"ATTRIBUTES_SMART_WORKER_PROMPT","55","asset","procurement","92","The output is comprehensive and follows all rules. I generated 82 attributes covering the full procurement lifecycle from requisition through receipt and capitalization, aligned with SAP MM/PM modules and NCDOT business context. All attributes have clear business value, proper naming (no product prefix except procurement_id), correct data types, appropriate classifications, and relevant references to GASB 34, SAP modules, NCGS, OMB Uniform Guidance, and other governing standards. I included fundamental transactional attributes (purchase_order_number, order_date, total_cost, procurement_status), vendor details, asset identification, financial tracking, location assignment, warranty management, and approval workflow. The schema reflects real SAP MM procurement fields while adding NCDOT-specific attributes for divisions, districts, federal funding programs, and DBE status. No semantic duplicates exist - each attribute serves a distinct business purpose. Minor uncertainty exists around whether all 82 attributes are strictly necessary versus comprehensive, but each has genuine business justification for asset procurement tracking in a government transportation agency context."
