"ATTRIBUTES_SMART_WORKER_PROMPT","83","environmental","nepa_document","92","The schema is comprehensive and covers all major aspects of NEPA documentation for transportation projects. It includes 82 attributes covering document identification, project details, environmental review processes, regulatory compliance (Section 404, Section 106, Endangered Species Act, Air Quality, etc.), public involvement, agency coordination, impacts assessment, mitigation, and administrative tracking. All attributes follow naming conventions (snake_case, no product prefix except for PK), use appropriate data types, include proper business glossary terms with full abbreviation expansions, and reference relevant governing bodies (NEPA, CFR Title 23, Clean Water Act, FHWA, etc.). Data classification tags are appropriately applied (confidential for estimated_project_cost, empty for non-sensitive operational data). The attribute count (82) is within the suggested range and reflects genuine business value aligned with NCDOT's environmental compliance domain. No semantic duplicates were identified. The schema aligns with ProjectWise and SharePoint as likely document management systems of record. Minor uncertainty exists around whether additional niche attributes (e.g., specific tribal consultation fields, detailed air quality pollutant measurements) should be included, but the current coverage represents the core comprehensive set that 95%+ of users would need."
