"ATTRIBUTES_SMART_WORKER_PROMPT","96","highway","service_request","92","The schema is comprehensive and follows all mandatory rules. It includes 73 attributes covering identification, classification, status tracking, location details, requester information, assignment and resolution tracking, cost and resource tracking, safety and traffic impact, SLA monitoring, and citizen feedback. All attributes have genuine business value aligned with NCDOT highway service request operations. Naming conventions follow snake_case without redundant product prefixes (except the PK). PII attributes are properly tagged as restricted with appropriate PII tags. Data types are valid Spark SQL types. The schema aligns with NCDOT operational systems (TIMS, SAP PM, GIS) and references appropriate governing bodies (FHWA, NEPA, AASHTO, NCGS). No semantic duplicates exist - lifecycle timestamps represent distinct events, target vs actual dates serve different purposes, and ID vs name fields are appropriately differentiated. The attribute count (73) is within the suggested range and represents comprehensive coverage without filler. Minor uncertainty exists around whether additional niche attributes (e.g., specific environmental compliance fields, detailed traffic control plan references) should be included, but the current set represents a balanced, production-ready model for highway service request management."
