"ATTRIBUTES_SMART_WORKER_PROMPT","99","highway","pavement_condition","92","The output provides comprehensive coverage of pavement condition assessment attributes aligned with FHWA HPMS standards, AASHTO pavement management practices, and NCDOT operational requirements. All 76 attributes have clear business value and are semantically distinct. The schema includes: (1) identification attributes (IDs, route, section, mileposts), (2) condition metrics (PCI, IRI, PSI, rutting), (3) distress measurements (cracking types, patching, potholes), (4) physical characteristics (surface type, age, lane configuration), (5) traffic data (AADT), (6) location data (county, division, GPS), (7) inspection metadata (date, crew, method, weather), (8) treatment recommendations, and (9) quality assurance fields. The model correctly maps to the Agile Assets (Bridge and Pavement Management) system mentioned in operational systems. All attributes follow naming conventions (no product prefix except PK, snake_case, semantic clarity). Data classifications are appropriately applied (inspector/reviewer names as confidential, cost data as confidential, operational data untagged). References align with FHWA, AASHTO, ASTM, and NCDOT standards. Minor uncertainty exists around whether certain niche attributes (video_log_reference, photo_reference_id) are universally used versus aspirational, but they represent reasonable pavement management practices. The attribute count (76) is well within the suggested range and reflects genuine business needs for comprehensive pavement condition tracking."
