"IN_DOMAIN_LINKING_SMART_PROMPT","11","asset","*","88","Complete analysis of all 11 products in the asset domain. All products are now connected with no silos. Candidate_evaluation was populated before links array with systematic evaluation of 35+ potential relationships. All 11 links in the output are genuine INCLUDE decisions with no SKIP/OMIT entries. No bidirectional violations, no self-references, no cross-domain links, no re-inclusion of existing FKs. Minor considerations: (1) Equipment location - noted in reasoning that business may need both assigned_location_id and current_location_id as separate FKs, but modeled as single location_id per standard practice; (2) Asset_inspection condition - retained condition_score as point-in-time numeric value while removing condition_rating STRING; (3) Warranty.asset_type_id was marked INCLUDE but on reflection may be premature without clear business requirement for warranty templates by type - however, it's a valid optional reference relationship. These are judgment calls within normal data architecture practice, not deficiencies. Output is structurally correct and complete."
"IN_DOMAIN_LINKING_SMART_PROMPT","12","project","*","88","Complete analysis of all 11 products in the project domain. All products are now connected with no silos. Identified 19 new FK relationships following normalization principles. Candidate_evaluation was populated before links array with all INCLUDE/EXCLUDE decisions documented. No self-referencing FKs, no bidirectional violations, no re-inclusion of existing FKs. Minor uncertainty on project_resource.project_schedule_id - marked as is_new_attribute=false assuming work_package_id implicitly references schedule, but this is a judgment call as the existing attribute list shows work_package_id as STRING not BIGINT FK. Also excluded project_milestone from having project_id since it appears to be a reference table of milestone types rather than transactional milestone instances - this is a reasonable interpretation but could be debated. Conservative on columns_to_remove for thin reference tables (project_phase, project_milestone) per lessons learned. One entry (project_document links to change_order/issue/risk) was considered but excluded from final output as those would be better modeled through a polymorphic document_reference pattern rather than multiple nullable FKs - this is a design judgment call. Overall output is structurally sound and follows all critical rules."
