"IN_DOMAIN_LINKING_SMART_PROMPT","15","safety","*","88","Complete analysis of all 7 products in safety domain. All links in the output array are genuine INCLUDE decisions from candidate_evaluation. No self-contradicting entries, no bidirectional violations, no existing FK re-inclusions, no cross-domain links, no self-references. All products are connected (no silos). Deducting 12 points for two judgment calls: (1) corrective_action.source_reference_number is a polymorphic string field - I added a dedicated incident_id FK rather than trying to normalize the polymorphic field itself, which is a design choice that could be debated; (2) safety_inspection.corrective_action_id assumes 1:1 or 1:N relationship (one inspection can generate one corrective action), but in reality one inspection might generate multiple corrective actions - this could potentially be M:N, though the visible schema suggests 1:N with corrective_action_required boolean. These are reasonable architectural decisions but involve some uncertainty. Overall output is structurally sound and follows all rules."
