"IN_DOMAIN_LINKING_SMART_PROMPT","18","planning","*","92","Complete analysis with all products evaluated systematically. All 9 products in the planning domain have been analyzed for FK relationships. The candidate_evaluation was populated BEFORE the links array, with clear INCLUDE/EXCLUDE decisions for each potential link. All 6 links in the output array were marked INCLUDE in candidate_evaluation - no self-contradicting entries. No bidirectional violations (no existing FKs provided to conflict with). No self-references. All targets are in-domain. Silo check passes - all products are connected through the proposed relationships: plan_status (incoming from plan), plan (incoming from planned_project, scenario, model; outgoing to plan_status), planned_project (outgoing to plan, corridor, funding_source), scenario (outgoing to plan), model (outgoing to plan), corridor (incoming from planned_project), funding_source (incoming from planned_project), stakeholder (no direct FK but flagged for M:N with plan), policy (no direct FK but flagged for M:N with plan). Three HIGH-confidence M:N relationships identified with strong business justification and 5+ relationship attributes each. Minor deduction (8 points) for: (1) stakeholder and policy remain without direct FK links, relying on M:N associations which are flagged but not yet implemented - this is architecturally correct but leaves them temporarily without hard links in the FK graph until association tables are created, and (2) some judgment calls on whether certain STRING reference fields (like model.scenario_name) should be normalized to FKs - conservative approach taken to avoid over-normalization of potentially multi-valued or version-reference fields."
"IN_DOMAIN_LINKING_SMART_PROMPT","19","highway","*","88","Complete analysis of all 10 products in highway domain. Candidate_evaluation populated BEFORE links array with systematic evaluation of all potential relationships. All 7 links in output array are genuine INCLUDE decisions from candidate_evaluation - no SKIP/OMIT entries. No bidirectional violations detected (verified each link against existing FKs and checked for reverse relationships). No re-inclusion of existing FKs. No self-references except the existing valid duplicate_of_request_id which was preserved. No cross-domain links (all targets are within highway domain). Silo check confirms all products now connected through the relationship graph. Two judgment calls noted: (1) sensor_reading.lane_id - included based on typical sensor deployment patterns where lane-specific monitoring is common, though not all sensors are lane-specific; (2) inspection_record.segment_id - included assuming bridge/structure inspections are segment-associated, though inspection_record attributes suggest structure focus rather than pavement. These are reasonable architectural decisions where domain experts could have different views. Columns_to_remove lists are conservative and verified against visible attributes. Minor uncertainty on whether roadway_classification should use roadway_classification_id or functional_class_code as FK name - chose roadway_classification_id for consistency with naming convention, though the link is semantically via functional_class_code. No rule violations detected."
