"LINK_MANY_TO_MANY_PRODUCTS_PROMPT","184","*","*","92","This is a strong M:N validation with clear evidence across all three required indicators: (1) Reciprocity is confirmed with specific, realistic government agency scenarios involving project-based work and grant funding - not theoretical but operational reality in public sector organizations; (2) Relationship data is confirmed with four explicitly identified attributes from the detection phase that clearly belong to the relationship itself; (3) Semantic name 'Cost Allocation' is a recognized financial accounting term. The business reality aligns with common government agency practices where employees split time across multiple funding sources and projects. I deducted 8 points for two considerations: (a) I added supplementary attributes (allocation_reason, audit fields) beyond the four explicitly identified in detection data, though these are standard for operational association tables in financial systems; (b) The domain choice reasoning could be slightly stronger - while Finance ownership is justified, HR could make a reasonable claim for shared ownership given the employee-centric nature of time allocation. Overall, this is a legitimate operational M:N relationship that meets all validation criteria with HIGH confidence appropriately assigned."
"LINK_MANY_TO_MANY_PRODUCTS_PROMPT","185","*","*","94","This is a textbook example of a valid M:N relationship in governmental accounting. The detection phase explicitly identified relationship-specific attributes (allocated_amount, allocation_date, fiscal_year, allocation_status, encumbrance_amount), which are core to governmental fund accounting. The business reality is clear: large transportation contracts are routinely funded from multiple sources (federal grants, state appropriations, bonds), and each fund can finance multiple contracts. The relationship has a recognized business name (Fund Allocation), is actively managed by finance staff, and requires tracking of allocation-specific data that belongs to neither the fund nor the contract alone. All validation tests pass with strong evidence. The association design includes only attributes that are either from the detection data or are standard governmental accounting requirements (expended_amount, remaining_balance, match_requirement_met). No speculative attributes were added. The domain assignment to finance is appropriate as fund accounting is a core finance function. All required fields are present, JSON structure is correct, and the model accurately represents NCDOT's governmental accounting reality."
"IN_DOMAIN_LINKING_SMART_PROMPT","25","grant","*","92","Complete analysis of all 8 products in the grant domain. All products now have relationships (no silos). Identified 10 genuinely missing in-domain FK links that establish the core grant lifecycle flow: program → application → award → disbursement/expense/compliance_check, with applicant as the master entity referenced throughout. All links follow proper directionality (child→parent), no bidirectional violations, no self-references, no cross-domain links, and no re-inclusion of existing FKs. Used candidate_evaluation properly before populating links array. Column removal recommendations are aggressive but validated against visible target table attributes. The domain already had extensive cross-domain FKs established, so this delta operation focuses on the missing in-domain structural relationships. Minor uncertainty on whether award.award_title should be removed (could be execution-specific vs. derived from application), but kept removal conservative. Score reflects thorough, rule-compliant analysis with proper use of the candidate_evaluation workflow."
"IN_DOMAIN_LINKING_SMART_PROMPT","26","rail","*","92","Complete analysis of all 9 products in rail domain. All products have connectivity (no silos). Identified 4 genuine new in-domain FK relationships with strong business justification. Used candidate_evaluation to pre-filter all potential links before populating links array - no SKIP/OMIT entries. No bidirectional violations (verified no reverse FKs exist). No existing FK re-inclusions (all 4 are genuinely new). No self-references. No cross-domain links. Column removal is conservative and validated against visible attributes. The signal_aspect removal from train_movement is a judgment call (it's a point-in-time value that could be kept), but normalizing to signal_type's aspect catalog is defensible for validation purposes. M:N analysis: rail domain relationships are primarily hierarchical (operator owns/operates segments, segments contain structures/crossings, movements traverse segments) - no genuine M:N patterns identified where both cardinality directions are true AND relationship data exists. Track_segment and train_schedule do NOT form M:N (schedules reference stations, not segments). Operator and track_segment do NOT form M:N (segments are owned/operated by one operator, though operators have many segments - this is 1:N). Minor uncertainty on whether signal_aspect should be removed (it's an event-specific observation), but the normalization is valid. Score reflects thorough, rule-compliant analysis with one borderline column removal decision."
"IN_DOMAIN_LINKING_SMART_PROMPT","27","dmv","*","88","Complete analysis of all 13 products in dmv domain. All products now have at least one relationship (inbound or outbound). Used candidate_evaluation to systematically evaluate all potential links before populating links array. No self-contradicting entries, no bidirectional violations, no existing FK re-inclusions, no cross-domain links, no self-references. All 13 links in output are genuine INCLUDE decisions. Minor uncertainty on two judgment calls: (1) whether vehicle should have FK to title (excluded due to bidirectional concern - title already points to vehicle, and vehicle can exist without title initially), (2) whether driver should have FK to current license (excluded because driver can have multiple licenses over time - this is 1:N from driver to license, not a single current license FK). These are reasonable architectural decisions where experts could disagree. Deducting 12 points for these borderline calls and the inherent complexity of temporal relationships in DMV domain (registrations, licenses, and titles all have renewal/replacement cycles that complicate simple FK modeling)."
"IN_DOMAIN_LINKING_SMART_PROMPT","28","project","*","92","Complete analysis of all products in the project domain. All 13 products now have relationships (inbound or outbound). Used candidate_evaluation to systematically evaluate all potential links before populating the links array. No self-contradicting entries, no bidirectional violations, no existing FK re-inclusions, no cross-domain links, no self-references. All links are genuine INCLUDE decisions with clear business justification. Conservative decisions made on several borderline cases (e.g., not linking project_issue.project_phase to project_phase because project_phase is a STRING field and the business may use flexible phase naming rather than strict FK enforcement). The project_milestone product is a reference table of milestone TYPES, not transactional milestone instances, so it correctly has only inbound FKs from other domains (acquisition_status, permit) and no in-domain child tables. The funding product represents consolidated funding allocations that may be unallocated or span multiple projects, so it correctly does not have a project_id FK. Minor uncertainty on whether project_resource.project_schedule_id is the optimal granularity (resources might be assigned at project level rather than schedule activity level), but the visible attributes (work_package_id, activity_id) suggest schedule-level assignment is the business reality. All 12 new links are operationally valid and improve normalization."
"IN_DOMAIN_LINKING_SMART_PROMPT","29","planning","*","88","Complete analysis of all products in the planning domain with systematic evaluation of all potential in-domain FK relationships. Successfully identified 4 new FK links that normalize STRING attributes to proper reference tables (plan_status, stakeholder). Properly used candidate_evaluation to assess all potential links before populating the links array, with no self-contradicting entries. All links in the array are genuine INCLUDE decisions with proper business justification and column removal specifications. Identified 2 HIGH-confidence M:N relationships (corridor-stakeholder, plan-stakeholder) with strong business justification and specific relationship attributes. One product (policy) remains siloed, which is acceptable for a master policy document reference table that may be linked via text references or external systems rather than direct FKs - no forced relationships were created. No bidirectional violations, no self-references, no cross-domain links, no re-inclusion of existing FKs. Minor uncertainty: The policy table silo could potentially be resolved if additional attributes were visible (e.g., if plan had a policy_id array or policy_references table), but based on visible attributes, no clear FK relationship exists. This is a reasonable conservative decision rather than a deficiency. Score reflects thorough, rule-compliant analysis with one acceptable siloed reference table."
"IN_DOMAIN_LINKING_SMART_PROMPT","30","hr","*","92","Complete analysis of all 18 products in hr domain. Used candidate_evaluation to systematically evaluate all potential links before populating links array. All 9 links in output were marked INCLUDE in evaluation. No bidirectional violations (verified each link against existing FKs). No self-referencing links. No cross-domain links. All target products exist within hr domain. Identified 3 genuine HIGH-confidence M:N relationships with strong business justification and 6+ relationship attributes each. All products are connected (no silos). Column removal recommendations are aggressive but validated against visible attributes in target tables. Minor uncertainty: employee.position_number is currently STRING - assuming it should be FK to position.position_id rather than position.position_number (using surrogate key pattern), but position table shows position_number as business key. This is a reasonable architectural decision either way. Deducting 8 points for this single judgment call on FK target (position_id vs position_number as target PK)."
"IN_DOMAIN_LINKING_SMART_PROMPT","31","grant","*","92","Complete analysis of all 8 products in the grant domain. All 10 identified links are genuine new relationships that establish the core transactional flow: program → application → award → disbursement/expense/compliance_check, with applicant as the central master entity. Used candidate_evaluation to systematically evaluate all potential links before populating the links array. No self-referencing links, no bidirectional violations, no cross-domain links, no re-inclusion of existing FKs. All columns_to_remove lists are validated against visible target table attributes. The domain now has complete connectivity with no siloed tables. Minor deduction (8 points) for the fact that I cannot see all attributes of target tables to verify 100% that every removed column truly exists in the target, but based on visible attributes and standard grant management data models, the normalization decisions are sound. All structural rules followed, output is production-ready."
"IN_DOMAIN_LINKING_SMART_PROMPT","32","dmv","*","92","Complete analysis of all 13 products in dmv domain. All potential FK relationships systematically evaluated in candidate_evaluation before populating links array. No self-contradicting entries, no bidirectional violations, no existing FK re-inclusions, no cross-domain links, no self-references. All 14 new links are genuine INCLUDE decisions with proper normalization (columns_to_remove populated based on visible attributes in target tables). Zero siloed products - every product has at least one relationship. Conservative on M:N detection - no genuine M:N relationships identified in this domain (most relationships are clear ownership/belonging patterns). Minor uncertainty on a few judgment calls: (1) whether vehicle should point to current registration vs registration pointing to vehicle - chose registration→vehicle as registrations are temporal/renewable, (2) whether driver should point to current license vs license pointing to driver - chose license→driver as licenses are temporal/renewable. These are reasonable architectural decisions where experts could differ slightly, but the chosen directions follow standard parent-child patterns. Deducting 8 points for these borderline cardinality decisions, though both are defensible."
"IN_DOMAIN_LINKING_SMART_PROMPT","33","planning","*","92","Complete analysis of all 11 products in the planning domain. All products have at least one relationship (inbound or outbound), achieving zero-siloed-tables requirement. Candidate_evaluation was populated before links array with systematic evaluation of 20+ potential relationships. All 7 links in output are genuine INCLUDE decisions with no SKIP/OMIT contradictions. No bidirectional violations, no self-references, no cross-domain links, no re-inclusion of existing FKs. Conservative decision on M:N relationships - while corridor↔stakeholder and policy↔plan could theoretically be M:N, the visible attributes don't show clear relationship data (dates, roles, amounts) that would justify M:N modeling, so kept as 1:N FKs for primary relationships. Column removal decisions are based on visible attributes and follow normalization principles. Minor uncertainty on whether mpo_list/rpo_list removal from corridor is appropriate if multiple stakeholders need tracking (would require M:N), but modeled the primary/lead stakeholder as 1:N FK which is a valid business interpretation. Score reflects thorough, rule-compliant analysis with conservative but defensible architectural decisions."
"IN_DOMAIN_LINKING_SMART_PROMPT","34","project","*","92","Complete analysis of all products in the project domain. All 13 products now have relationships (inbound or outbound). Used candidate_evaluation to systematically evaluate all potential links before populating the links array. No self-contradicting entries, no bidirectional violations, no existing FK re-inclusions, no cross-domain links, no self-references. All 21 links in the array are genuine INCLUDE decisions. Conservative on M:N detection - no genuine M:N relationships identified in this domain (project_stakeholder_engagement and project_funding are already modeled as association products). Minor uncertainty on whether to add project_phase_id FKs to products that already have phase_code/project_phase STRING columns - chose to add FKs only where the phase reference is clearly to the phase definition (change_order, schedule) and not add where the STRING field may contain free-text phase descriptions. This is a reasonable judgment call. Columns_to_remove lists are conservative - only removing columns where the target table clearly contains the data."
"IN_DOMAIN_LINKING_SMART_PROMPT","35","hr","*","88","Complete analysis of all hr domain products with systematic evaluation of FK candidates. All 15 new links are genuine INCLUDE decisions with proper business justification. No self-contradicting entries, no bidirectional violations, no existing FK re-inclusions, no cross-domain links, no self-references. Candidate_evaluation was populated before links array as required. Minor uncertainty on 2 links: (1) employee.position_number → position.position_number assumes position_number is a natural key match (not position_id PK), which is reasonable given the attribute naming but involves a judgment call about whether position_number is unique/indexed; (2) training_record.certification_earned and crew_assignment.certification_type link to certification table assuming string matching to certification.name or certification.code, which is operationally realistic but involves judgment about the matching strategy. These are reasonable architectural decisions, not errors. No M:N relationships identified as hr domain relationships are primarily hierarchical (employee→position→department, employee→grade, etc.). All products now connected through employee as central hub. Scoring 88% to reflect the two judgment calls on string-based FK matching, but these are valid design decisions in the absence of explicit surrogate key columns."
