"DOMAIN_METRICS_SMART_PROMPT","1","bridge","*","92","The output is comprehensive and follows all structural rules. All metric views are sourced from valid products (bridge, inspection_record, cost_item) with existing columns. Every dimension and measure includes clear business-focused comments. Type safety is strictly enforced—only NUMERIC_ALLOWED columns are used in arithmetic and aggregates. No nested aggregates are present. All measures pass the six self-validation questions: they are executive-relevant (structurally deficient rate, poor condition rate, safety concern rate are federal MAP-21 performance measures used by FHWA and state DOT leadership), action-triggering (overdue inspection rate drives compliance actions, safety concern rate triggers emergency response), steering-meeting-fit (these metrics appear in quarterly business reviews and board decks), outcome-linked (tied to safety, compliance, cost, and federal funding), decision-gap-filling (removing these would leave gaps in performance evaluation), and pass the 'so what?' test (e.g., 'We care about structurally deficient rate because it determines federal funding eligibility and public safety risk'). The metrics are high-value, compound (rates, percentages, averages), and value-driven (cost, condition, compliance). Minor deduction: A few dimension expressions (e.g., year_built_decade) involve type casting that could be simplified, and one measure (poor_condition_bridge_count) uses a complex CASE with multiple OR conditions that could theoretically be split for clarity—but these are judgment calls, not rule violations. The output is production-ready and business-meaningful."
