"DOMAIN_METRICS_SMART_PROMPT","19","procurement","*","92","Output is comprehensive and follows all rules. All metric views are high-value, compound, and decision-oriented (contract performance, vendor diversity, payment efficiency, vendor performance evaluation). All measures pass the six self-validation questions. Type safety is strictly enforced - only NUMERIC_ALLOWED columns used in arithmetic/aggregates. No nested aggregates. All expressions are valid Databricks SQL. All source products, columns, and dimensions exist in the provided context. JSON structure is correct with all required fields. Minor deduction: Could have included one additional metric view for goods_receipt to track receiving efficiency and quality inspection metrics, which would be valuable for supply chain operations. However, the six views provided are all high-impact and production-ready."
"DOMAIN_METRICS_SMART_PROMPT","20","safety","*","92","Output is comprehensive and follows all structural rules. All metric views are sourced from valid products in the safety domain. All dimensions and measures use only columns that exist in the provided schema and respect the Type Matrix (NUMERIC_ALLOWED vs DIMENSION_ONLY). No nested aggregates are present. All measures pass the six self-validation questions for executive relevance, action triggers, steering meeting fit, outcome linkage, decision gaps, and the 'so what?' test. Metric selection is focused on high-value, compound, and value-driven KPIs (crash rates, fatality reduction, response times, completion rates, goal achievement rates, benefit-cost ratios) that directly inform safety program investment, HSIP funding allocation, IMAP deployment, corrective action prioritization, and regulatory compliance decisions. Minor judgment calls were made on which specific crash types and contributing factors to include as dimensions (selected the most strategically relevant ones), and on grouping certain status values in CASE expressions (used reasonable business logic for 'completed' vs 'open' states). These are standard data architecture decisions, not deficiencies. All JSON structure is valid, all required fields are present, and all comments are business-meaningful. Score reflects high confidence in correctness and business value, with minor deduction for inherent judgment calls in dimension selection and status grouping logic."
